the edge accepts up to 2,000 characters; the golden set's 120 questions
are 11 tokens at the median and 33 at the longest

  2,000 characters of    accepted  bytes  tokens  billed   encode
  English prose               yes  2,004     667     667    0.2ms
  digits                      yes  2,000     807     807    1.1ms
  Chinese characters          yes  6,000   3,869   3,869    0.9ms
  emoji                       yes  8,000   4,493   4,493    0.6ms
  one accent, repeated        yes  3,999   2,000   2,000    0.3ms
  mixed scripts               yes  5,307   3,084   3,084    0.8ms

  billed = the API's prompt tokens, less 6 for the message itself

Every model call resends the question. Over the 13 calls a max_steps=12 run
can make, the question alone uses this much of the run's 60,000-token budget:
  a median golden question        13 x    11 =    143 tokens,  0.2%
  2,000 characters of emoji       13 x 4,493 = 58,409 tokens, 97.3%
